      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"input & output in Python\"\n",
        "author: \"Tony Duan\"\n",
        "\n",
        "execute:\n",
        "  warning: false\n",
        "  error: false\n",
        "format:\n",
        "  html:\n",
        "    toc: true\n",
        "    toc-location: right\n",
        "    code-fold: show\n",
        "    code-tools: true\n",
        "    number-sections: true\n",
        "    code-block-bg: true\n",
        "    code-block-border-left: \"#31BAE9\"\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "Data input and output in Python\n",
        "\n",
        "![](images/1_-OQi5hp-uoL_KdIydr4hew.gif){width=\"500\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "# input\n",
        "\n",
        "Data input is the process of reading data from external sources into your Python program. This section covers common file formats and methods for reading data.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Read CSV"
      ],
      "id": "fa43e0d5"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Import the pandas library for data manipulation\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "# Read the CSV file 'data/Book3.csv' into a pandas DataFrame\n",
        "data=pd.read_csv('data/Book3.csv')\n",
        "# Display the DataFrame\n",
        "data"
      ],
      "id": "f80dee26",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Read CSV online"
      ],
      "id": "d1dd8e30"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| eval: false\n",
        "# Import the pandas library\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "# Define the URL of the CSV file\n",
        "url='https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rfordatascience/tidytuesday/master/data/2020/2020-02-11/hotels.csv'\n",
        "# Read the CSV file from the URL into a pandas DataFrame\n",
        "hotels=pd.read_csv(url)"
      ],
      "id": "b1b26dca",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Read Excel\n",
        "\n",
        "sheet_name=0 read first sheet.\n",
        "\n",
        "sheet_name=1 read second sheet.\n",
        "\n",
        ".sheet_name='Sheet1' read 'Sheet1' sheet."
      ],
      "id": "7af5194c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Import the pandas library\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "# Read the Excel file 'data/Book1.xlsx' into a pandas DataFrame, specifying the first sheet (index 0)\n",
        "data_excel=pd.read_excel('data/Book1.xlsx',sheet_name=0)\n",
        "# Display the DataFrame\n",
        "data_excel"
      ],
      "id": "139db0cc",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Read Parquet\n",
        "\n",
        "Parquet format is one of the best for data analytics."
      ],
      "id": "989c5567"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Import the pandas library\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "# Read the parquet file 'data/df.parquet' into a pandas DataFrame\n",
        "data= pd.read_parquet(\"data/df.parquet\")\n",
        "# Print the shape of the DataFrame (number of rows, number of columns)\n",
        "data.shape"
      ],
      "id": "d6fb9db3",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Display the first 5 rows of the DataFrame\n",
        "data.head()"
      ],
      "id": "f56ab487",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Read gzipped Parquet"
      ],
      "id": "418336ab"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Import the pandas library\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "# Read the gzipped parquet file 'data/df.parquet.gzip' into a pandas DataFrame\n",
        "data= pd.read_parquet(\"data/df.parquet.gzip\")\n",
        "# Print the shape of the DataFrame\n",
        "data.shape"
      ],
      "id": "3064e0af",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Read Feather"
      ],
      "id": "dab1d1fb"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Import the pandas library\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "# Read the feather file 'data/feather_file.feather' into a pandas DataFrame\n",
        "data=pd.read_feather(\"data/feather_file.feather\")\n",
        "# Display the first 5 rows of the DataFrame\n",
        "data.head()"
      ],
      "id": "9a12061d",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Text Files"
      ],
      "id": "eabbb290"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Open the file 'txt_example.txt' in read mode\n",
        "f = open(\"txt_example.txt\", \"r\")\n",
        "# Read the entire content of the file into variable a\n",
        "a=f.read()\n",
        "# Print the content\n",
        "print(a)"
      ],
      "id": "2036e130",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Output\n",
        "\n",
        "Data output involves writing data from your Python program to external files. This section demonstrates how to save data in various formats.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Write CSV"
      ],
      "id": "23000ee3"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Write the first 5 rows of the DataFrame to a CSV file named 'data/out.csv', without including the index\n",
        "data.head().to_csv('data/out.csv', index=False)  "
      ],
      "id": "96264384",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Write Excel"
      ],
      "id": "1a2c946f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Write the data_excel DataFrame to an Excel file named 'data/out.xlsx'\n",
        "data_excel.to_excel('data/out.xlsx')"
      ],
      "id": "3e493f0b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Write Parquet"
      ],
      "id": "b78d3df8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Write the first 100 rows of the DataFrame to a parquet file named 'data/df.parquet'\n",
        "data.head(100).to_parquet('data/df.parquet') "
      ],
      "id": "b77f3133",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Output to zip format"
      ],
      "id": "ed73dd7f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Write the first 100 rows of the DataFrame to a gzipped parquet file named 'data/df.parquet.gzip'\n",
        "data.head(100).to_parquet('data/df.parquet.gzip',\n",
        "              compression='gzip')  "
      ],
      "id": "ca75ceda",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Write Feather"
      ],
      "id": "a1cb0ea7"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Write the first 100 rows of the DataFrame to a feather file named 'data/feather_file.feather'\n",
        "data.head(100).to_feather(\"data/feather_file.feather\")"
      ],
      "id": "e641f758",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Write Text File"
      ],
      "id": "af5610c0"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Define a multi-line string\n",
        "a_txt='''\n",
        "Testing\n",
        "\n",
        "Testing,  Testing.\n",
        "Testing\n",
        "'''\n",
        "\n",
        "# Print the string\n",
        "print(a_txt)"
      ],
      "id": "34562981",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Open the file 'myfile.txt' in write mode\n",
        "f = open(\"myfile.txt\", \"w\")\n",
        "# Write the content of a_txt to the file\n",
        "f.write(a_txt)\n",
        "# Close the file\n",
        "f.close()"
      ],
      "id": "593f53be",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Reference\n",
        "\n",
        "https://medium.com/@gadhvirushiraj/the-best-file-format-for-data-science-ed756f937be8"
      ],
      "id": "b74c4724"
    }
